WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.210
- [Narrator] This year's midterm elections

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.970
could tip the balance
of power in Congress.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.910
Republicans need net
gains of one Senate seat

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.110
and four House seats,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.390
to take control of both chambers.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.370
- During midterm elections
a lot is at stake,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.600
but most importantly

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.130
the most watched thing here in Washington

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.290
is the battle for the control of Congress.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.540
- [Narrator] WSJ National
Politics Reporter,

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.650
Joshua Jamerson,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.930
explains how Democrats and Republicans

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.670
have been shaping the conversation

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.730
around the economy,
abortion, gun violence,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.860
immigration and student loan forgiveness,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.813
with the goal of persuading voters.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.280
Americans are feeling
the pain of inflation

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.700
as they face the biggest price
increases in four decades.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.160
- Grocery bills, gas
prices, things like that,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.920
where money is impacting
people's everyday lives.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.709
I would say that is definitely
something I hear from voters

00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:52.440
when I'm traveling on the campaign trail.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.910
- [Narrator] Some Republican candidates,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.497
including Senator Ron Johnson,

00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:57.840
who is seeking reelection in Wisconsin,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.360
claim that the party
controlling Washington now

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.580
is responsible for rising prices.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.740
- Democrats are printing
trillions of dollars

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.500
to pay for their massive
depths of spending.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.860
Inflation is the Democrat's
tax on the middle class.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.950
- That's what you hear
mostly from Republicans,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.755
is that simply by curtailing

00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:19.350
what Joe Biden Democrats
are able to spend,

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.289
that our presence in
Washington in majorities

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:24.406
would have a positive
impact on your finances.

00:01:24.406 --> 00:01:25.596
- [Narrator] Democrats have countered

00:01:25.596 --> 00:01:28.410
that there is more at work
when it comes to inflation

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.480
than just government policies.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.810
Candidates, including Georgia
Senator, Rafael Warnock,

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.190
point to supply chain issues

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.540
and their willingness to take on

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.370
what they see as price gouging.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.560
- What if I told you
shipping container companies

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.690
have been making record profits,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.050
while prices have been
skyrocketing on you?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.090
That's why I'm pushing
to hold them accountable.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.370
- Democrats have tried to explain this

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.464
and explain how they might use

00:01:51.464 --> 00:01:53.520
some of those inflationary pressures.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.650
But there's a saying in politics,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.690
that it's a lot harder to explain,

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.070
and if you're explaining,

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.100
you're already starting not
in a position of strength

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.703
and that's something the
Democrats have tried to combat.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.430
- [Narrator] The leak of a
Supreme court draft opinion,

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:09.930
signaling the court's intention

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.370
to overturn Roe V. Wade,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.960
made abortion a campaign issue

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.320
even before the court released
its decision in late June.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.620
- That definitely rippled
across the campaign trail.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.116
I happened to be in Georgia,

00:02:21.116 --> 00:02:23.520
with a few Republican candidates there,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.990
and they immediately started talking

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.750
about how this was a
victory for the Republicans.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.040
- [Narrator] Republican leaders argued

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.360
that this long sought victory

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.280
will energize their own voters.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.339
- The argument to voters was

00:02:33.339 --> 00:02:36.000
this is what your vote
for Republicans got,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.950
this long held decade-long effort

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.320
to get constitutional originalists

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.000
with more of a conservative view

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.340
on the Supreme court to
make these decisions.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.800
- [Narrator] Democrats are
hoping this will inject urgency

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.358
into the midterm elections.

00:02:48.358 --> 00:02:50.403
- A woman's right to choose,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.520
reproductive freedom,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.830
is on the ballot in November.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.390
- [Narrator] A survey of American adults

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.510
shows increased support
for abortion access.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.520
According to a WSJ poll,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.830
some 57% of respondents

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.740
said a woman should be able
to obtain legal abortions

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.850
for any reason.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.700
- How that relates to a political
issue is a big question,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.680
and one that I don't think
we'll get an answer to

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.513
until November

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.630
- [Narrator] A string of
mass shootings in the U.S.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.448
reignited the debate around
laws to curb gun violence

00:03:21.448 --> 00:03:23.220
and has led to the passage

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.802
of the first major federal
change to gun laws in decades.

00:03:26.802 --> 00:03:29.870
- God willing.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.913
This is going to save a lot of lives.

00:03:31.913 --> 00:03:33.114
- [Narrator] While many
congressional Democrats

00:03:33.114 --> 00:03:36.030
support aspects of the
bipartisan legislation,

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.160
that includes funding for red flag laws

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.660
and mental health programs,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.090
some don't think the
package goes far enough.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.860
- Now, of course, this bill doesn't do

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.120
everything we need,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.440
not by a mile,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.620
we all understand this is a compromise.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.480
- Democrats generally would agree

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.280
that universal background checks

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.810
is something that they would like to see.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:55.710
And then underneath that,

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.128
there's some support for
banning certain assault weapons.

00:03:59.128 --> 00:04:00.420
(gunshot in distance)

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.190
- [Narrator] But many
congressional Republicans

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.140
have insisted that Democrats' efforts

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.520
to change U.S. gun laws

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.660
or further restrict access to
firearms is not the answer.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.184
- Their so-called solutions

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:15.750
wouldn't have stopped these mass murders.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.010
And they know this

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.090
- In addition to issues of shared interest

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.010
among Republicans and Democrats,

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.250
the two parties also have
their individual focuses.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.530
Republican candidates
are betting immigration

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.270
is one voters care about.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.490
Republican representative, Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.500
who is the front runner
to become House Speaker,

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.660
if the party wins control in November,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.523
argues the Biden administration's
immigration policy

00:04:39.523 --> 00:04:42.778
has allowed dangerous
drugs to flow into the U.S.

00:04:42.778 --> 00:04:46.710
- Fentanyl is now the number one killer

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.073
to Americans between
the ages of 18 and 45.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.430
There is no longer a few border cities.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.640
Every city in America
is now a border city.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.650
- It really is about this idea

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.050
that the Southern border is porous,

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.510
and Democrats won't stop people

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.970
from illegally crossing into the country.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.020
- [Narrator] Democrats, however,

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.750
have been talking about
student loan forgiveness.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.583
As a candidate,

00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:13.320
President Biden proposed forgiving $10,000

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.170
of federal student loan
debt, per borrower.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.913
- Democrats remember that,

00:05:17.913 --> 00:05:18.746
and they're kind of disappointed

00:05:18.746 --> 00:05:19.920
that it hasn't happened yet.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.300
- [Narrator] Biden is likely to decide

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.910
on a student loan forgiveness
plan later this summer,

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.360
aimed in part at motivating
young voters to cast ballots.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.610
But some Republicans are
betting this will backfire

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.160
and be met with resentment
from many voters.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.530
Many also argue that
forgiving student loan debt

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.220
would add to the national debt
and further fuel price rises.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.115
- Republicans counter

00:05:39.115 --> 00:05:42.280
the economy is already really really hot,

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.340
and canceling student loan debt

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.053
could just add more inflation.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.280
Republicans will say if
you send us to Washington,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.080
if you give us control of
the House that's in it,

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.353
we can act as a check on
this Joe Biden presidency.

